# Vendored pstack

These skill directories, except `verify-blattwerk/`, are a copy of
`pstack/skills/` from https://github.com/cursor/plugins.

- commit: eb4db2b55b2b7dec3d9282754cddf0a56bf4ff10
- version: 0.15.30 (`pstack/plugin.json` and `pstack/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`)
- license: `pstack/LICENSE`, copied here as `PSTACK-LICENSE` (MIT, Lauren Tan)

`verify-blattwerk/` is Blattwerk's own verification skill. It is not part of pstack.
`agents/` from the plugin is not vendored.

## Refresh to latest upstream

From a clean checkout of `cursor/plugins` at `main`:

```sh
git clone --filter=blob:none --sparse --depth 1 --branch main https://github.com/cursor/plugins.git /tmp/plugins-pstack
git -C /tmp/plugins-pstack sparse-checkout set pstack
git -C /tmp/plugins-pstack rev-parse HEAD
python3 -c 'import json; print(json.load(open("/tmp/plugins-pstack/pstack/plugin.json"))["version"])'
```

In this repo, replace every skill directory except `verify-blattwerk/`, refresh the license, and rewrite the commit and version lines in this file:

```sh
python3 - << 'PY'
import shutil
from pathlib import Path
src = Path("/tmp/plugins-pstack/pstack/skills")
dst = Path(".cursor/skills")
keep = {"verify-blattwerk", "PSTACK-LICENSE", "PSTACK-VERSION"}
upstream = {p.name for p in src.iterdir() if p.is_dir()}
for p in dst.iterdir():
    if p.name in keep or not p.is_dir():
        continue
    if p.name not in upstream:
        shutil.rmtree(p)
for name in sorted(upstream):
    target = dst / name
    if target.exists():
        shutil.rmtree(target)
    shutil.copytree(src / name, target, copy_function=shutil.copy2)
shutil.copy2("/tmp/plugins-pstack/pstack/LICENSE", dst / "PSTACK-LICENSE")
PY
```

Then set `commit` to the `rev-parse` output and `version` to the `plugin.json` version, and commit. Do not add CI, cron, or workflow files for the refresh.
